 like `_TEMPERATURE_WITHDRAWN_LOGGED` keyed on the resolved string), and state whether 'once' means per-process or per-run so step 6 and its test agree.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design: 'Writing it for hosted OpenAI emits a once-per-run deprecation notice'","Edit-set 6: 'emit the cfg:openai-chat notice once when resolved is hosted openai-chat:'","_deprecations.warn_deprecated always emits (log/warning/stderr) with no dedup: `(logger or _DEFAULT_LOGGER).warning(msg)`","runner.py already uses a module-level `_TEMPERATURE_WITHDRAWN_LOGGED: set[str]` precisely to make a per-model log fire once, evidence the naive path fires per-call","Testing asserts 'the deprecation notice fires once for hosted openai-chat:'"],"finding":"The plan asserts the openai-chat: deprecation notice fires 'once per run' / 'once' but does not specify the dedup mechanism, and the referenced warn_deprecated helper performs no de-duplication — it emits on every call, and runner.run() is invoked once per op (multiple ops per workflow run).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6a9cd5bc0f28d045","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design ('once-per-run deprecation notice'); Edit-set step 6; Testing ('the deprecation notice fires once')","norm_id":"neebb466f0d052205","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A plan-review or completion run drives several run() calls (Pass-1, Pass-2/verify, verifier) all on hosted openai-chat:, emitting the deprecation notice repeatedly instead of once","The 'fires once' test passing per-process vs per-run is ambiguous without a stated dedup key"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In step 6, guard the warn_deprecated('cfg:openai-chat') call behind a module-level dedup set in runner.py (mirroring _TEMPERATURE_WITHDRAWN_LOGGED, keyed on `resolved`), and define 'once' as once-per-process-per-resolved-string; align the Testing assertion accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either add an acceptance criterion that exercises the `openai-responses:` default against the live OpenAI Responses API (or a named smoke), OR record an explicit rationale that the landed contract tests + the closed research verdict (ageless-ferny-ugandakob) constitute sufficient live-boundary coverage and no further live exercise is warranted.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'all new tests run in-process against an httpx.MockTransport stub with no network or provider credentials'","AC2: 'The contract tests are re-run against the migrated paths and the behavioural diff is recorded (structured output, streaming, tool calls, retries, custom base URLs)' — these are the MockTransport contract tests","E6(f): a proving command that passes on a mock/offline substitute which BYPASSES the new behavior does not prove the criterion"],"finding":"The plan cuts hosted OpenAI over to `openai-responses:` (pydantic-ai builds OpenAIResponsesModel against the live OpenAI Responses API) by default, but every new/re-run test runs against an httpx.MockTransport stub with no network or credentials; no acceptance criterion exercises the migrated path against the live Responses endpoint, and the plan does not state a rationale for that absence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa1157dd07d2ca65d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design 'Portability' paragraph + Testing section + AC line 2","norm_id":"nbf6e46332ddb14a1","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The Responses API wire shape diverges from the MockTransport stub in a way the contract fixtures don't model (e.g. streaming event framing, tool-call payload), and the cutover ships a live regression that green offline tests never catch"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short rationale to the Testing/Portability section noting the research ticket already validated Responses-readiness against pydantic-ai 1.107.2's advertised OpenAIResponsesModel contract, so the MockTransport contract tests are the accepted behavioural-diff evidence and a live-endpoint exercise is deliberately out of scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance assertion that a hosted-OpenAI cfg under DEFAULT resolution (no explicit qualifier) results in pydantic-ai constructing an OpenAIResponsesModel and issuing a /v1/responses-shaped request against the MockTransport — binding the resolution flip to the actual model type built, not just the resolver's output string.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'hosted openai:/gpt-4o -> openai-responses:' asserts the resolver output string only","'Re-run the landed contract tests (already parameterized over both prefixes) as the wire-level behavioural diff' — the contract tests are parameterized over prefixes independently of which prefix the default resolution now selects","Design: 'the runner leaves it a lazy string for pydantic-ai to build OpenAIResponsesModel' — the seam between resolution output and the actual model type built is the defaulted path"],"finding":"For a cutover that makes openai-responses: the DEFAULT for hosted OpenAI, the testing plan asserts resolution (string equals openai-responses:) and separately re-runs contract tests parameterized over both prefixes, but does not name an assertion binding the two: that a hosted-OpenAI cfg under DEFAULT resolution actually causes pydantic-ai to build an OpenAIResponsesModel (vs. an OpenAIChatModel). A green resolution-string test plus an independently-parameterized contract test can both pass without ever proving the default flip drives a Responses build end-to-end.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f56be47876af89817","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"T